Z||000001||phillip||03-24-2000||12:52 PM||||looking in an old kit car mag. it says get the uncut wiring harness,tranny(i guess that would depend on if it matches your preference),all sensors and computer,engine mounts,air cleaner,and air conditioning if desired. if its got the five speed and you don't want it get it any way if you can. you WILL find a buyer.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Dan86gt3.8||03-24-2000||04:20 PM||||Yes phiil is right.  I was informed to get,engine,tranny (if you want it)all accesorys (ie altenator, a/c pump, ignition ie, the coil packs) uncut engine wiring harness all the way back to the computer, the computer itself, if it has an electronic auto get the wiring to it, the adl (its the diagnostic link, forgot what it stands for but its what a mechanic or you can tap into, to get to the computer to get trouble codes).  Also get the part of the exhaust system that bolts to the y pipe, you cut most of the factory pipe off and just use that flange to start your exhaust system.  thats all I can think of for now.  if i rember anything else I will let you know!||||reg||1
