Z||000011||lowCG||03-26-2000||10:28 PM||||Here's what I've come to know about the 3.4TDC swap;<P>Water filler/thermostat housing must be adapted,and probably the heater hoses also need to be routed differently.<P>Exhaust must be fabricated from the Y-pipe,which now faces towards the rear.<P>Passenger side hinge must be trimmed.<P>Motor mounts aren't a problem,need to drill one hole somewhere on the subframe.<P>Flywheel needs to be nuetrally balanced.I'll be lightening mine also.Pretty sure I'm going to use a Luk clutch,at least the plate,might use another disc.<P>Power steering pump must be removed and have an idler bearing put in it's place.The same bearing as used on the timing belt works fine.<P>The fuel lines must be re-routed to meet the fuel rail on the 3.4.<P>Every wire that has anything to do with the engine controls must be re-routed for the new ECM,engine combo.<P>Air cleaner is large enough on the Fiero,just need to adapt the hose to the new(huge)throttle body.<P>Can do this all myself,so there's no kit to buy,just motor,hoses,spark plugs($8 each!),belts,muffler($200),clutch$2-300).I might split the tranny and replace the final drive bearings if it needs to be done.The performance chip will be a Christmas present.<P>Tomorrow it's off to the carwash for an underside de-greasing on the hoist for a few $,and I'll watch from a safe distance.<P>Good thing I'm starting early in the season,huh? <BR><p>[This message has been edited by lowCG (edited 03-26-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||Formula||03-27-2000||10:21 PM||||Does the tdc use a hi-po header or is it like the fiero's factory manifold.  If I spend the money on a 3.4 I would like to get a sweet sounding exhaust too.  Maybe Camaro headers into flowmasters or something,  How much do plan on spending on exhaust, and can you go a little bit more in depth about the water-filler/heater hose adaption?<P>Would you mind posting some links to 3.4 swaps if you have them handy?||||reg||1
Z||000013||lowCG||03-28-2000||12:18 AM||||Well all the links I've found are dead,so I'm going from recent advice,and memory.<BR>As for the exhaust,that is changing from a $210 nice sounding large muffler,to a Flowmaster that is advertised to have "an agressive resonance",because of space  limitations.Oh well,It's alot cheaper this way.The factory manifolds are quite large,and will be just fine,and making the dream headers with 2"dia., balanced primaries would be more work than the rest of the swap, really aren't needed with the mere 9.25:1 compression that it now has,if I were to rebuild it,it'd get some 11:1 pistons,four valve engines work great with some compression.The donor car has a 2-1/2" pipe after the Y. Hey Batboy,if you're reading,see what your DesktopDyno comes up with for a 4valve,11:1,ported/polished head 3.4L V6. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Just for fun.||||reg||1
